<title>ZIMBABWE: Zimbabwe's Rothmans boosts half-yr shr.</title>
<headline>Zimbabwe's Rothmans boosts half-yr shr.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year ended September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	 (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>- including income from</p>
<p>	associated companies	     146.5   vs   113.5</p>
<p>- excluding income from</p>
<p>	associated companies		99.5   vs   83.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)				 33.0   vs   18.0</p>
<p>    Operating income			20.7   vs   18.2</p>
<p>    Div income				 1.2   vs   0.9</p>
<p>    Pre-interest income		   21.9   vs   19.1</p>
<p>    Interest paid			    0.3   vs   0.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax income			  21.6   vs   18.7</p>
<p>    Taxation				   7.7   vs   7.0</p>
<p>    After-tax income			13.9   vs   11.7</p>
<p>Equity adjustment: Shr of income</p>
<p>    retained by associated companies   6.6   vs   4.1</p>
<p>    Attrib. income			  20.5   vs   15.9</p>
<p>    Turnover				 134.7   vs   111.4</p>
<p>Div payable December 6 on register November 7.</p>
<p>Full name: Rothmans of Pall Mall (Zimbabwe) Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - With private consumption spending expected to increase during the next six months, the company said it anticipated a three percent rise in volumes on the domestic market for the year.</p>
<p>It, however, said firmer tobacco leaf prices and increased costs of imported raw materials would adversely affect margins during the next six months, thereby offsetting some of the benefits of volume growth. A satisfactory increase in attributable earnings for the year was expected.</p>
<p>----Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9----</p>
